+## Final reading and limited prose changes
+
+I read the full Introduction and applied abstract, the updated
+project/notation/writer rules and the target outline. The definitions,
+marked-vanishing reduction, normalization domains and two proof routes
+remain coherent. The mathematical and precision statements need no
+revision.
+
+Three small changes have a concrete purpose:
+
+- The opening names the first Hodge class, removing the ambiguous
+  shorthand first class.
+- The transition to the last two results says their indices grow
+  with genus, rather than calling them the opposite range.
+- The interpretation paragraph identifies the fixed insertion list
+  of the second theorem separately from the fixed defect of the
+  fourth. The previous blanket sentence about all insertion indices
+  could be mistaken as covering the growing top index. The paragraph
+  keeps the absent inverse-genus term, cubic dependence, two powers
+  per unit of defect, transport factorial and lack of a final relative
+  error rate.
+
+The stable-graph route, independent top-class route, ILW transport,
+Appendices A/B and shorter reading path already describe the completed
+article accurately. No broad rewrite, new mathematical claim or
+symbol is warranted.
+
+## Additional primary-source attribution
+
+I read https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35492v5 and the official HTML
+https://arxiv.org/html/2610.35492v5 at Theorem 1.1 and
+(11.6)--(11.7). The added background citation credits its broader
+absolute-volume result, including the unmarked coefficients.
+The Introduction says that A reconstructs only the particular
+second coefficient needed here. No priority is claimed and no
+new proof dependency is introduced. The old W26 key and its
+v4 Lemma 7.2/Appendix C.1 locators are unchanged.
